invalid "-custom" must be followed by s string encoding maximum HLS resolution choices:
   Uxplay restricts HLS video streams to a maximum resolution height 2160p at 60fps.
   If your system cannot decode this fast enough, you can set a lower limit for each codec.
   The codecs allowed are AVC (h264), HEVC (h265), VP9, AV1, and you can set a common limit
   for streams at 30 fps and 60 fps, or separate limits, for each.

   For example, the "custom profile" string
                  "HEVC:1440,720; VP9:1080; AV1:0"
   allows HEVC streams with resolution height up to 1440p @ 30fps or 720p @ 60fps, VP9 streams
   up to 1080p @ 60 fps, and excludes streams with the AV1 codec, with no restrictions on AVC.

   The string length is limited to 64 characters: empty space between codec entries (as in the
   example above) is ignored (enclose the string in quotes if it includes empty spaces).

